\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A16}{\ignorespaces Every inferential statistic computed for this paper, in one place. Conventions are defined in the text immediately above: \emph  {Welch} is a two-sided unequal-variance $t$ on per-seed arm means, \emph  {perm.} an exact permutation test over seed relabellings, \emph  {Wilcoxon} a two-sided signed-rank test on paired per-parent values ($93$ parents). $\Delta $ is the difference of arm means (or, for the Wilcoxon rows, the median paired shift). Seed counts are completed seeds. This table is a completeness record and nothing in the paper is stated in terms of it; the corresponding descriptive results are in \Cref  {tab:primary,tab:scaleseeds,tab:p0seeds}. No $p$-value is corrected for multiplicity, degrees of freedom are small throughout, and every row involving a value-carrying cell is conditional on completion (\Cref  {app:stability}).\relax }}{44}{table.caption.79}}
